herdr
=====

Guides: herdr-1-basics, herdr-2-panes, herdr-3-agents, herdr-4-config.

herdr 0.9.5. The prefix is C-b. <prefix> c means: press C-b, release, then press c.

  <prefix> ?                      Show every active binding (/ filters)

PANES
  <prefix> v                      Split right
  <prefix> -                      Split down
  <prefix> h/j/k/l                Focus the pane left/down/up/right
  <prefix> Tab / <prefix> S-Tab   Cycle panes
  <prefix> S-h/j/k/l              Swap panes
  <prefix> z                      Zoom the focused pane
  <prefix> r                      Enter resize mode
  <prefix> x                      Close the pane
  <prefix> S-p                    Rename the pane
  <prefix> e                      Open the scrollback in an editor

COPY MODE
  <prefix> [                      Enter copy mode
  h/j/k/l, w/b/e, C-u/C-d         Move
  / or ?                          Search forward / backward (n / N repeat)
  v or Space                      Start a selection
  y or Enter                      Copy
  q or Esc                        Leave copy mode
  Mouse drag                      Copy without copy mode

TABS
  <prefix> c                      New tab
  <prefix> S-t                    Rename the tab
  <prefix> S-x                    Close the tab
  <prefix> n / <prefix> p         Next / previous tab
  <prefix> 1..9                   Jump to a tab

WORKSPACES AND AGENTS
  <prefix> w                      Workspace navigation (Esc leaves)
  <prefix> g                      Goto picker for every agent and terminal (/ search;
                                  b/w/i/d filter blocked/working/idle/done; a all)
  <prefix> b                      Toggle the sidebar (spaces and agents panel)
  <prefix> o                      Jump to the pane of the latest notification
  <prefix> S-n                    New workspace
  <prefix> S-w                    Rename the workspace
  <prefix> S-d                    Close the workspace
  <prefix> S-g                    New git worktree workspace

SESSION
  <prefix> q                      Detach. The server and agents keep running
  <prefix> S-r                    Reload config
  <prefix> s                      Open settings
  herdr                           Launch or attach
  herdr --remote desk --remote-keybindings server
                                  Attach from the laptop (server keys and plugins)
  herdr session list / herdr session attach <name>
                                  List / attach sessions
  herdr server stop               End the session and stop all panes

DRIVE OTHER AGENTS
Read IDs from the JSON output. Never derive them from sidebar order.

  herdr pane current | herdr pane list | herdr agent list
  herdr pane split --current --direction right --no-focus
  herdr pane run <pane> "<command>"   # sends text and Enter
  herdr pane read <pane> --lines 50
  herdr pane wait-output <pane> --match "done" --timeout 60000
  herdr agent start <name> --kind claude --pane <pane>   # kinds include kiro, codex, claude, pi
  herdr agent prompt <agent> "<text>" --wait --timeout 600000
  herdr agent wait <agent> --until idle
  herdr agent read <agent> --lines 80
  herdr agent send-keys <agent> esc
  herdr agent attach <agent>

LIAISON PATTERN
One agent drives others with the herdr skill.

  Start the liaison agent inside a herdr pane. The skill checks HERDR_ENV=1.
  Name herdr in the prompt, or the skill does not load. Example: "Use herdr to start a
    claude reviewer in a pane to the right and give it this task: ..."
  A blocked worker waits at an approval prompt. The liaison asks you. Answer in that pane.
  <prefix> g then b               List blocked agents
  After a timeout or agent_prompt_stalled, check herdr agent read before you resend.
